course: dictionary
lesson: 1753
title: Clatter: a sound you can hear
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like what they mean. «Clatter» is one of them: say it aloud and it rattles, just like the noise it describes. A word that copies a sound is called onomatopoeia.
explain: To clatter means to make a loud, rattling noise as hard things bang against each other, like falling pans or shoes on stairs. A clatter is that noise itself. «The tray hit the floor with a clatter» names the sound.
explain: Clatter can also mean moving noisily: «The horses clattered down the stone street.» The words around it, such as stone street and hard hooves, show that it means moving with a loud, rattling sound.
fact: To clatter means to make a loud, rattling noise.
fact: A clatter is the loud, rattling noise itself.
fact: Onomatopoeia is a word that sounds like its meaning.
fact: «White storks clatter their bills to greet each other.» Storks make this sound with their beaks.
fact: To clatter somewhere means to move there noisily, as in «clatter down the stairs».
exercise: What does «clatter» mean in a kitchen full of falling pans? | *A loud, rattling noise | A quiet whisper | A soft, gentle hum | A pleasant smell
exercise: «The clatter of plates filled the school canteen.» What is a clatter here? | A quiet room | A person who cooks | A kind of plate | *A loud, rattling noise
exercise: «Shoebills greet each other by clattering their huge beaks.» What does clattering their beaks make? | They fall asleep | They hide under water | Their beaks go soft | *A loud, rattling sound
test: What is onomatopoeia? | A kind of bird | *A word that sounds like its meaning | A type of hard floor | A word for slow movement
test: «The horses clattered down the stone street.» Clattered means | flew up into the sky | stopped completely and stayed silent | fell asleep in the road | *moved down the street with a loud, rattling noise
exam: In «Storks hardly have a voice; they greet each other by clattering their bills like a wooden toy», what does the comparison to a wooden toy suggest? | A soft, sleepy sound | No sound at all | A tune played on a piano | *A sharp, rattling sound
